--- machine\system\console
canonical: Machine\System\Console

The machine's virtual consoles: the text screens on its own display and
keyboard (`/dev/tty1` and so on). Not a terminal over SSH or a serial line,
and not the desktop, whose keyboard is the browser's.

Default security: inherits the Machine hive root (SYSTEM and Administrators
full, Authenticated Users read).

--- machine\system\console keymap
canonical: Machine\System\Console Keymap
type: REG_SZ
default: (absent — the kernel's built-in US layout)
valid: a keymap name under /usr/share/kbd/keymaps, such as uk, de, fr or dvorak; a name, never a path
applies: restart of the console-keymap service, and every boot

The console's keyboard layout. The `console-keymap` service loads it at
boot with `loadkeys`; to apply a change at once, restart the service
(`svctl restart console-keymap`), which System Settings does for you.

One layout serves every virtual console: the kernel holds a single keymap.
A name that is not a keymap leaves the layout as it was, and the service
logs why.
